    "updated_at": "2018-02-01T01:26:32Z",
    "body": "Reviving, because @annevk reminded me about the `Headers` constructor which is still hand-rolling taking a map-sequence, which is super non-obvious when you read it.\r\n\r\nAs an argument type: `map-sequence<Foo, Bar>` does the same processing as `sequence<>`, but ensures that (a) each item in the sequence is an Infra \"pair\" containing a Foo and a Bar.  Your algorithm receives it as an Infra list of pairs.\r\n\r\nAs a return type: the returned value must be an Infra list, containing only Infra pairs where the first item is of type Foo and the second is of type Bar; it transforms into a JS Array of Arrays.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
