    "created_at": "2019-07-16T22:59:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-16T23:00:17Z",
    "body": "Oh, and there is [a place](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/31057dd8cf48866512863c3efcae39e34d5243e8/spec/index.bs#L235) where we already are trying to define a tuple today, to do an ES6-style multiple-return.\r\n\r\nI think if we had typed tuples in WebIDL, it would mostly solve both issues:\r\n`tuple<GPUBuffer, ArrayBuffer>`\r\n`sequence<tuple<DOMString, Buffer>>`\r\n[`sequence<tuple<unsigned int, GPUVertexBufferDescriptor>>`](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/186/files#diff-7d154c8abbb1fb80041e213976224980R502)\r\n\r\nThough it would not express the uniqueness of keys.",
